-- title:
--   The weighted Schatten logarithm
-- statement:
--   For operators $\rho,\sigma$ and a real parameter $t$, define
--   $$
--   g_{\rho,\sigma}(t)=\log\left\|\rho^{1/2}\sigma^{t-1/2}\right\|_{1/t}.
--   $$
--   The powers use continuous functional calculus and the norm is the trace-defined Schatten expression. The logarithm is natural. For faithful density states $\rho,\sigma$ on a nonzero finite-dimensional complex Hilbert space, and $\alpha>0$, $\alpha\ne1$, the exact secant identity uses $t=1/(2\alpha)$:
--   $$
--   D_\alpha(\rho\Vert\sigma)=\frac{-g_{\rho,\sigma}(1/(2\alpha))}{(1/(2\alpha)-1/2)\log2}.
--   $$ Conversion to bit-valued state divergence is a separate division by $\log 2$. The raw expression uses Lean's totalized powers, reciprocals, and real logarithm.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/JWang226/Continuity-of-regularized-channel-renyi-divergence/blob/e29274a69978bb499f00497481c6008befb0b84d/QuantumChannelContinuity/StateOrderRenyi.lean#L27-L28

